ADDITIONAL DISCLAIMER — AI-GENERATED SECURITY AUDITS

This software is a skill/prompt framework that directs AI assistants to
perform automated security analysis. All audit findings, vulnerability
assessments, remediation suggestions, and generated code produced through
the use of this skill are the output of an AI model and are provided solely
as informational suggestions.

1. NO SECURITY GUARANTEE. The authors and copyright holders do not warrant
   that this skill will detect all, or any, security vulnerabilities present
   in an application. Security audits performed by AI models may miss
   critical issues, produce false positives, or generate incomplete results.

2. NO LIABILITY FOR SECURITY INCIDENTS. The authors and copyright holders
   shall not be liable for any security breach, data leak, unauthorized
   access, loss of data, financial loss, regulatory penalty, or any other
   harm — direct or indirect — resulting from the use of this skill, from
   acting on its recommendations, or from failing to detect vulnerabilities
   in audited applications.

3. NOT A SUBSTITUTE FOR PROFESSIONAL SECURITY REVIEW. This skill does not
   replace a qualified security professional, penetration tester, or
   certified auditor. Critical systems, systems handling personal data, or
   systems subject to regulatory compliance (LGPD, GDPR, PCI-DSS, HIPAA,
   etc.) must be reviewed by qualified human experts before going to
   production.

4. AI MODEL LIMITATIONS. Security recommendations generated by AI models
   may be incomplete, incorrect, or based on outdated threat intelligence.
   The authors do not guarantee the accuracy or completeness of any
   security analysis produced through this skill.

5. GENERATED CODE RISK. Any code modifications or remediations suggested or
   applied by this skill must be reviewed, tested, and validated by the end
   user before deployment. Applying AI-generated security patches without
   human review may introduce new vulnerabilities or break existing
   functionality.

6. USER RESPONSIBILITY. By using this skill, you acknowledge that you are
   solely responsible for the security of your own applications, for
   validating all outputs of this skill, and for all decisions made based
   on its recommendations.

